	setcycle 49 condition ""
	setcycle 49 Condition_Num ""
	setcycle 49 comprehension_q ""
	setcycle 49 booklet ""
	setcycle 50 passage ""
	setcycle 50 line ""
	setcycle 50 line_text "One caller records that Robert Browning was 'simple, natural, and <br/>playful,' and that Mrs. Browning was all 'genius and sensibility.'"
	setcycle 50 probe ""
	setcycle 50 condition ""
	setcycle 50 Condition_Num ""
	setcycle 50 comprehension_q ""
	setcycle 50 booklet ""
	setcycle 51 passage ""
	setcycle 51 line ""
	setcycle 51 line_text "Daytimes Browning walked forth with Elizabeth's little dog Flush, but<br/>he seldom could be lured from his home evenings. "
	setcycle 51 probe ""
	setcycle 51 condition ""
	setcycle 51 Condition_Num ""
	setcycle 51 comprehension_q ""
	setcycle 51 booklet ""
	setcycle 52 passage ""
	setcycle 52 line ""
	setcycle 52 line_text "One privileged intruder, coming frequently at night to join the poets<br/>over hot chestnuts and mulled wine, found talk good and laughter plentiful."
	setcycle 52 probe ""
	setcycle 52 condition ""
	setcycle 52 Condition_Num ""
	setcycle 52 comprehension_q ""
	setcycle 52 booklet ""
	setcycle 53 passage ""
	setcycle 53 line ""
	setcycle 53 line_text "During the third year of their stay in Italy, a son, Robert Weidemann<br/>Browning, was born."
	setcycle 53 probe ""
	setcycle 53 condition ""
	setcycle 53 Condition_Num ""
	setcycle 53 comprehension_q ""
	setcycle 53 booklet ""
	setcycle 54 passage ""
	setcycle 54 line ""
	setcycle 54 line_text "But through this happy life a strain of dark foreboding began to <br/>creep. "
	setcycle 54 probe ""
	setcycle 54 condition ""
	setcycle 54 Condition_Num ""
	setcycle 54 comprehension_q ""
	setcycle 54 booklet ""
	setcycle 55 passage ""
	setcycle 55 line ""
	setcycle 55 line_text "Elizabeth Browning’s father died unrelenting in his disavowal of her <br/>marriage, refusing to see her or to sanction any of his family to see her. "
	setcycle 55 probe ""
	setcycle 55 condition ""
	setcycle 55 Condition_Num ""
	setcycle 55 comprehension_q ""
	setcycle 55 booklet ""
	setcycle 56 passage ""
	setcycle 56 line ""
	setcycle 56 line_text "Three children all younger than her own boy were left to her by a <br/>dearly beloved sister who died. "
